D JOURNAL OF MEDICINE DESCRIBES PRELIMINARY RESULTS OF REMDESIVIR TRIAL MADE PUBLIC BY NIAID ON APRIL 29."}{'symbol': 'GILD', 'date': '2020-05-22 14:30:00', 'title': 'ANTHONY FAUCI SAYS INITIAL STUDY OF MODERNA VACCINE ENCOURAGING - CNBC', 'text': ':U.S. INFECTIOUS DISEASE EXPERT ANTHONY FAUCI SAYS INITIAL STUDY OF MODERNA VACCINE ENCOURAGING'}{'symbol': 'MCD', 'date': '2020-05-22 18:30:00', 'title': "MCDONALD'S SETS QUARTERLY CASH DIVIDEND OF $1.25/SHARE", 'text': 'SETS QUARTERLY CASH DIVIDEND OF $1.25PER SHARE.'}{'symbol': 'MRNA', 'date': '2020-05-22 14:30:00', 'title': 'ANTHONY FAUCI SAYS INITIAL STUDY OF MODERNA VACCINE ENCOURAGING - CNBC', 'text': ':U.S. INFECTIOUS DISEASE EXPERT ANTHONY FAUCI SAYS INITIAL STUDY OF MODERNA VACCINE ENCOURAGING'}{'symbol': 'TAP', 'date': '2020-05-22 20:30:00', 'title': 'MOLSON COORS FURLOUGHING CERTAIN EMPLOYEES IN EUROPE AND NORTH AMERICA HOSPITALITY UNITS', 'text': "MOLSON COORS BEVERAGE CO - ON MAY 21 BOARD DETERMINED THAT IT WILL SUSPEND ITS REGULAR QUARTERLY DIVIDENDS ON ITS CLASS A AND CLASS B COMMON SHARES.MOLSON COORS - MOLSON COORS CANADA ALSO DETERMINED ON MAY 21 THAT IT WILL SUSPEND REGULAR QTRLY DIVIDENDS ON ITS CLASS A & CLASS B EXCHANGEABLE SHARES.MOLSON COORS BEVERAGE CO - REDUCING PLANNED 2020 CAPITAL EXPENDITURES BY APPROXIMATELY $200 MILLION.MOLSON COORS BEVERAGE CO - FURLOUGHING CERTAIN EMPLOYEES IN COMPANY'S EUROPE BUSINESS AND NORTH AMERICA HOSPITALITY BUSINESSES.MOLSON COORS BEVERAGE - ACTIVELY EVALUATING VARIOUS EUROPEAN GOVERNMENT LIQUIDITY PROGRAMS POTENTIALLY AVAILABLE TO COMPANY AND ITS SUBSIDIARIES."}{'symbol': 'NVDA', 'date': '2020-05-22 18:30:00', 'title': 'NVIDIA SETS QUARTERLY CASH DIVIDEND OF $0.16/SHARE', 'text': 'NVIDIA ANNOUNCES QUARTERLY CASH DIVIDEND TIMING.SETS QUARTERLY CASH DIVIDEND OF $0.16PER SHARE.'}{'symbol': 'PCG', 'date': '2020-05-22 22:30:00', 'title': 'PG&E CORPORATION ANNOUNCES FINAL VOTING RESULTS ON PLAN OF REORGANIZATION', 'text': "ANNOUNCES FINAL VOTING RESULTS ON PLAN OF REORGANIZATION.VOTING WILDFIRE VICTIMS OVERWHELMINGLY SUPPORT PG&E'S PLAN.CONFIRMATION HEARING SCHEDULED TO BEGIN MAY 27, 2020 IN BANKRUPTCY COURT.VOTING CERTIFICATION REFLECTS THAT PLAN WAS ACCEPTED BY IN EXCESS OF 85% IN BOTH NUMBER AND AMOUNT OF WILDFIRE VICTIMS WHO CAST VOTES ON PLAN.FINAL VOTING RESULTS HELP COMPANY STAY ON TRACK TO GET ITS PLAN CONFIRMED BY JUNE 30, 2020."}{'symbol': 'SYY', 'date': '2020-05-22 19:30:00', 'title': 'SYSCO DECLARES QUARTERLY DIVIDEND PAYMENT', 'text': 'SYSCO DECLARES QUARTERLY DIVIDEND PAYMENT.SETS REGULAR QUARTERLY CASH DIVIDEND OF $0.45PER SHARE.'}{'symbol': 'UAL', 'date': '2020-05-22 20:30:00', 'title': 'UNITED AIRLINES TO PAY CEO SCOTT KIRBY AN ANNUAL BASE SALARY OF $1 MLN', 'text': 'UNITED AIRLINES HOLDINGS INC - COMPENSATION COMMITTEE APPROVED AN ANNUAL COMPENSATION PACKAGE FOR SCOTT KIRBY WITH AN ANNUAL BASE SALARY OF $1 MILLION.UNITED AIRLINES - TARGET ANNUAL INCENTIVE PROGRAM OPPORTUNITY EQUAL TO 250% OF BASE SALARY FOR SCOTT KIRBY WAS APPROVED.UNITED AIRLINES - TARGET LONG-TERM INCENTIVE (“LTI”) OPPORTUNITY EQUAL TO TEN TIMES BASE SALARY FOR SCOTT KIRBY WAS APPROVED.UNITED AIRLINES - FOR PRESIDENT BRETT HART, COMPENSATION COMMITTEE APPROVED ANNUAL BASE SALARY OF $775,000.UNITED AIRLINES - FOR HART, APPROVED TARGET AIP OPPORTUNITY EQUAL TO 175% OF BASE SALARY.UNITED AIRLINES - FOR HART, APPROVED TARGET LTI OPPORTUNITY EQUAL TO 7.5 TIMES BASE SALARY.UNITED AIRLINES - BASED ON NEW COMPENSATION LEVELS, COMPENSATION COMMITTEE APPROVED, GRANTED LTI AWARDS OF $2.3 MILLION FOR KIRBY, $1.8 MILLION FOR HART.UNITED AIRLINES -  MAY 2020 LTI AWARDS FOR CEO SCOTT KIRBY AND PRESIDENT BRETT HART ARE IN FORM OF TIME-VESTED RESTRICTED STOCK UNITS.UNITED AIRLINES - NEW BASE SALARY, TOTAL COMPENSATION LEVELS APPROVED FOR SCOTT KIRBY AS CEO ARE LOWER THAN LEVELS FOR PRIOR CEO OSCAR MUNOZ.UNITED AIRLINES - ACKNOWLEDGES THAT DUE TO PSP AGREEMENT LIMITATIONS, KIRBY & HART MAY NOT REALIZE FULL VALUE OF RESPECTIVE COMPENSATION PACKAGES.UNITED AIRLINES - BASE SALARY, TOTAL COMPENSATION LEVELS APPROVED FOR HART AS PRESIDENT ARE LOWER THAN LEVELS FOR KIRBY IN HIS ROLE OF PRESIDENT.'}